{
  "_comment": [
    "Competitive tiers, used as the primary input to Pokémon pricing.",
    "",
    "FORMAT: DOUBLES (VGC). Champions is a doubles game — 4v4, bring six pick four — and the",
    "doubles meta is very different from singles. op.gg ranks the two separately: Salamence is",
    "#1 in singles and #3 in doubles, Rillaboom #1 in doubles. Always take the Double tab.",
    "",
    "DERIVED FROM RANKS, NOT PUBLISHED TIERS. op.gg publishes a single ordered ladder rather",
    "than letter tiers, so the bands below are cut by rank position: the top 18 are S, the next",
    "35 A+, and so on. Every asset is ranked, so nothing falls to UR — see `defaultTier`.",
    "",
    "FORMS COLLAPSE TO THE ASSET, BEST RANK WINS. op.gg ranks Wash Rotom (#68) apart from Fan",
    "Rotom (#249), but only the species is tradable here, so Rotom takes #68. Same for",
    "Basculegion and Indeedee, where only one sex is any good.",
    "",
    "Careful with regional forms: op.gg *displays* Hisuian forms under the bare species name —",
    "\"Arcanine\" is both #18 (arcanine-hisui) and #112 (arcanine) — so the two must be told apart",
    "by slug, not by the name shown. They are separate assets here and must not be swapped.",
    "",
    "Edit freely: this is the commissioner’s balance lever, and house rules beat any public",
    "ranking. Names are matched case-insensitively against each roster entry’s species name,",
    "regional-form label, Mega label and alternate-form label. Anything that fails to match is",
    "reported by `npm run roster:build` rather than ignored, so typos surface immediately.",
    "",
    "`baseTiersIncludeMegas` stays true: op.gg ranks a species as it is actually played, which",
    "includes Mega-evolving it, so a Mega must not promote its species a second time."
  ],
